      "bio": "Lois Jane Frankel (/ˈfræŋkəl/ FRANG-kəl; born May 16, 1948) is an American politician and lawyer who has been the United States representative for Florida's 22nd congressional district since 2023, having previously served it from 2013 to 2017. As a member of the Democratic Party, she represented the 21st congressional district from 2017 to 2023, was a 7-term member of the Florida House of Representatives, and was mayor of West Palm Beach for two terms.",
      "campaign_website": "http://frankel.house.gov",
      "key_messages": [
        "Frankel supported President Trump's 2017 decision to recognize Jerusalem as Israel's capital, stating it is consistent with U.S. law and affirms Jerusalem as the capital of Israel and the Jewish people.",
        "Frankel supports gun control measures including high-capacity magazine bans, universal background checks, bump stock bans, and repealing the Dickey Amendment to allow CDC research on gun violence prevention."
      ],
      "campaign_themes": [
